@begin(section)

@title(Get dsolv)

@begin(section)
@title(Install)

dsolv is a Common Lisp program. It is not yet on
@link[uri="https://quicklisp.org"](Quicklisp) or
@link[uri="https://github.com/ocicl/ocicl"](OCICL) as a published system. To
use it, clone @link[uri="https://github.com/djha-skin/dsolv"](the source
code) and build the executable:

@begin[lang=sh](code)
git clone https://github.com/djha-skin/dsolv.git
cd dsolv
ocicl install          # install the dependencies listed in ocicl.csv
./scripts/build        # build the ./com.djhaskin.dsolv executable
@end(code)

The @c(./scripts/build) script bakes in the large heap and control-stack sizes
needed for big repository resolutions (for example, the 19 MB APT
@c(Packages.gz) index exercised by the test suite). Override the sizes with
the @c(DYNAMIC_SPACE_SIZE) and @c(CONTROL_STACK_SIZE) environment variables
if your use case needs different values.

The resulting binary is called @c(com.djhaskin.dsolv). Rename it or symlink it
into your @c(PATH) so you can invoke it as @c(dsolv):

@begin[lang=sh](code)
ln -s "$PWD/com.djhaskin.dsolv" ~/.local/bin/dsolv
@end(code)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Code)

dsolv lives out on
@link[uri="https://github.com/djha-skin/dsolv"](Github). It is built on the
@link[uri="https://github.com/djha-skin/cliff"](CLIFF) framework, which
handles argument parsing, configuration files, and environment variables;
@link[uri="https://github.com/djha-skin/svers"](svers) provides the version
comparison algorithms; and @link[uri="https://github.com/djha-skin/nrdl"](NRDL)
provides the data format used for configuration and output.

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Support and Problems)

If you have a hard time using dsolv to resolve dependencies within builds, it
is a bug! Please do not hesitate to let the authors know via a
@link[uri="https://github.com/djha-skin/dsolv/issues"](GitHub issue).

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Contributions)

Please contribute to dsolv!
@link[uri="https://github.com/djha-skin/dsolv/pulls"](Pull requests) are most
welcome. Please have a look at the @c(Contributing) page first.

@end(section)

@end(section)
